        "anchor": "prologue",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Factual Prologue"
          }
        ]
      },
      "description": {
        "units": [
          {
            "id": "u-001755",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "The factual prologue distinguishes lived experience, eyewitness testimony, documentary evidence, disputed findings, and later interpretation. Adjudication may determine what a lawful authority concludes from that evidence; it does not determine whether an experience occurred. Readers are not asked to accept an attribution of responsibility without examination. Competing accounts should be tested against the same record."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
