  "home": {
    "units": [
      {
        "id": "u-001747",
        "type": "prose",
        "role": "introduction",
        "units": [
          {
            "id": "u-001748",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "This is a patient-authored publication about what it means to seek and provide care when illness, disability, trauma, uncertainty, and medical authority meet. It brings together factual context, essays, artwork, sound, an Atlas of ethical principles, and practical resource paths for patients, clinicians, families, educators, researchers, advocates, and anyone trying to make care more truthful, accessible, and humane."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "u-001749",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "The reader is not asked to accept a disputed conclusion in advance. The factual material distinguishes evidence from interpretation; the essays examine what responsible conduct may require; the Atlas and ethics architecture connect those questions to medical ethics, human rights, spiritual practice, disability access, and systems of care."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "u-001750",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "A difficult case can become a place where patients and clinicians learn how to preserve truth, dignity, agency, care, and the possibility of correction. Suffering does not need to be enlarged into crisis to deserve careful attention."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "u-3f0a8c11",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Start with a path that matches what you need:"
